.TH UNIQ 1.SH NAMEuniq \- drop repeated lines.SH SYNOPSIS\fBuniq\fR[\-u] [\-d] [\-c] [\-\fIn\fR] [^\fIn\fR] input.SH DESCRIPTION\fBuniq\fRreads a file and writes one copy of each run of identical adjacentlines.  Only ADJACENT lines are compared, so sort the file first totreat every repeat alike..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-u\fRonly the lines that are not repeated..TP 12\fB\-d\fRone copy of only the lines that are repeated..TP 12\fB\-c\fRevery line once, with the number of times it occurred in front..TP 12\fB\-\fIn\fRskip the first\fIn\fRblank-separated fields before comparing..TP 12\fB^\fIn\fRthen skip\fIn\fRcharacters more..SH EXAMPLES.nfsort names > s; uniq s         each name onceuniq -c s                      and how oftenuniq -1 log                    ignoring the first field of each line.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOsort